From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:58:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Fix drone and fighter movement, recall to bay and stack
 launches

- DestinyManager::Orbit: negate the unsigned follow distance as a float. The
  uint32 wraparound placed orbiting objects ~170,000 km away, so fighters warped
  back to their target over and over (also affects NPC orbits).
- Drones fly at their real maxVelocity from launch, so the client is told the
  right speed; idle orbit changes only the speed fraction.
- Agile objects (agility < 2s) turn straight to their target point; Turn()
  steers toward the current direction to the target point.
- Drop: stop launching a dragged stack at the pilot's drone limit.
- Guard Orbit()/SetSpeedFraction() against an orbit target already removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GZgkReFMTa8JWavQEivVUA
